---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const locale = "en" as const;
const title = "Privacy policy · WEBAO";
const description = "How WEBAO collects, uses and deletes personal information: forms, billing, site analytics, outreach and connected ad accounts.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} locale={locale} pageKey="privacy">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell" style="max-width: 860px;">
      <div class="eyebrow">Policy</div>
      <h1 class="display" style="font-size: var(--text-h1); margin-top:12px;">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="prose" style="margin-top:14px; max-width: 60ch;">
        What we collect, why we collect it, and how to get it deleted.
        Written in plain language, because that is the only kind worth
        reading. Last updated: October 23, 2026.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-top: 36px; display:grid; gap: 20px;">
        <div style="border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:16px; padding:24px; background: var(--card-bg);">
          <h2 style="font-size:17px; letter-spacing:-0.01em; margin:0 0 12px;">Who we are</h2>
          <p class="prose" style="font-size:14px; margin:0;">
            Webao is a website studio based in Montreal, Canada. This policy
            covers webao.ca, the sites we build and host for clients, and the
            services we run for them. Questions about privacy go to
            <a href="mailto:contact@webao.ca" style="color: var(--accent-text);">contact@webao.ca</a>.
            The person responsible for the protection of personal information
            at Webao is the owner, reachable at that address.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:16px; padding:24px; background: var(--card-bg);">
          <h2 style="font-size:17px; letter-spacing:-0.01em; margin:0 0 12px;">Messages you send us</h2>
          <p class="prose" style="font-size:14px; margin:0;">
            When you use the contact, support or start form, we receive the
            details you enter, such as your name, email, phone number,
            business name and your message. A copy lands in our email inbox
            and the submission is kept in our system so we can reply, follow
            up and keep a record of the request. We use it only to handle
            what you asked about. We do not add you to a mailing list.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:16px; padding:24px; background: var(--card-bg);">
          <h2 style="font-size:17px; letter-spacing:-0.01em; margin:0 0 12px;">Clients, billing and payments</h2>
          <p class="prose" style="font-size:14px; margin:0;">
            If you buy from us, we keep your name, email, business details,
            what you purchased and your billing status, so we can run your
            site and your account. Payments are processed by Stripe. Your
            card details go to Stripe directly and never pass through our
            servers. Stripe tells us whether a payment succeeded, so we know
            where your account stands.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:16px; padding:24px; background: var(--card-bg);">
          <h2 style="font-size:17px; letter-spacing:-0.01em; margin:0 0 12px;">Visits to this site</h2>
          <p class="prose" style="font-size:14px; margin:0 0 12px;">
            We measure our own traffic with our own tool. There are no
            third-party trackers on webao.ca and no advertising cookies.
            When you visit, we record:
          </p>
          <ul class="prose" style="font-size:14px; margin:0; padding-left:18px; display:grid; gap:6px;">
            <li>The pages you view, how long you stay, and the links and buttons you click on our site</li>
            <li>The page you arrived from, your device type and browser</li>
            <li>Your country and city, worked out from your IP address, which is stored with the visit</li>
            <li>Your language and light or dark theme preference</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="prose" style="font-size:14px; margin:12px 0 0;">
            Visits are tied to a random session number kept in your browser,
            not to your name. Session records delete themselves after 365
            days. We look at this data in aggregate to see which pages are
            useful and to fix problems. Your theme, language, cart contents
            and the session number itself are stored in your browser's local
            storage, on your device, not in tracking cookies.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:16px; padding:24px; background: var(--card-bg);">
          <h2 style="font-size:17px; letter-spacing:-0.01em; margin:0 0 12px;">Business outreach</h2>
          <p class="prose" style="font-size:14px; margin:0;">
            We find the businesses we write to, and their public contact
            details, from public sources such as their own listings and
            directories. If we email a business, we record whether the links
            in that email were clicked and whether it got a reply. We keep
            this so we can honor opt-outs and never write again to a business
            that said no. Reply to any outreach email and ask us to stop, and
            we stop.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:16px; padding:24px; background: var(--card-bg);">
          <h2 style="font-size:17px; letter-spacing:-0.01em; margin:0 0 12px;">Accounts you connect with us</h2>
          <p class="prose" style="font-size:14px; margin:0;">
            Some services involve connecting accounts you own, for example a
            Meta or Google advertising account. With your authorization, we
            receive data from those platforms, such as campaign results and
            leads sent through your ads. We use it only to manage and report
            on your advertising, as you instruct. You can cut the access at
            any time in the platform's own settings, and you can ask us to
            delete what we received, as described below.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:16px; padding:24px; background: var(--card-bg);">
          <h2 style="font-size:17px; letter-spacing:-0.01em; margin:0 0 12px;">Who processes data for us</h2>
          <p class="prose" style="font-size:14px; margin:0 0 12px;">
            A short list of providers runs parts of the service, and each one
            only gets what it needs to do its job:
          </p>
          <ul class="prose" style="font-size:14px; margin:0; padding-left:18px; display:grid; gap:6px;">
            <li>Cloudflare: hosting, storage and email delivery for the site</li>
            <li>Stripe: payment processing</li>
            <li>Google: our email inbox</li>
            <li>SMTP2GO: sending email from our addresses</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="prose" style="font-size:14px; margin:12px 0 0;">
            We never sell personal information. Apart from the providers
            above, we disclose information only when the law requires it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:16px; padding:24px; background: var(--card-bg);">
          <h2 style="font-size:17px; letter-spacing:-0.01em; margin:0 0 12px;">How long we keep it</h2>
          <p class="prose" style="font-size:14px; margin:0;">
            Visit records delete themselves after 365 days. Messages and
            client records are kept while you are a client and for a
            reasonable period after, and some billing records have to be kept
            longer because tax and accounting law requires it. Outreach
            records, including opt-outs, are kept so we can respect them. If
            you ask us to delete your information, we delete everything we
            are not required to keep.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:16px; padding:24px; background: var(--card-bg);">
          <h2 style="font-size:17px; letter-spacing:-0.01em; margin:0 0 12px;">Your rights</h2>
          <p class="prose" style="font-size:14px; margin:0;">
            You can ask what personal information we hold about you, get a
            copy of it, have it corrected, and ask us to delete it. You can
            also withdraw consent to our use of it. Write to
            <a href="mailto:contact@webao.ca" style="color: var(--accent-text);">contact@webao.ca</a>
            and we will answer within 30 days. If we cannot settle your
            concern, you can contact the Commission d'accès à l'information
            du Québec.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="data-deletion" style="border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:16px; padding:24px; background: var(--card-bg); scroll-margin-top: 100px;">
          <h2 style="font-size:17px; letter-spacing:-0.01em; margin:0 0 12px;">Delete your data</h2>
          <p class="prose" style="font-size:14px; margin:0;">
            To have your data deleted, email
            <a href="mailto:contact@webao.ca" style="color: var(--accent-text);">contact@webao.ca</a>
            from the address concerned and tell us what to delete, for
            example a form submission, your client record, or data received
            from a connected platform such as Meta. We delete it within 30
            days, except for records the law requires us to keep, and we
            confirm by email when it is done.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:16px; padding:24px; background: var(--card-bg);">
          <h2 style="font-size:17px; letter-spacing:-0.01em; margin:0 0 12px;">Security and changes</h2>
          <p class="prose" style="font-size:14px; margin:0;">
            The site runs over HTTPS, access to our systems is limited to the
            owner, and our providers run their own security programs. No
            system is perfect, so if a privacy incident involving your
            information ever happens, we will notify you and the authorities
            as the law requires. If this policy changes, the new version goes
            on this page with a new date at the top.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
